            <ArticleTitle>Occupational asthma from tafenoquine in the pharmaceutical industry: implications for QSAR.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>256-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/occmed/kqu193</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report occupational asthma and rhinitis in a formulation pharmacist, employed in the development of tafenoquine. Tafenoquine is a new anti-malarial drug in development; the pure drug substance has an asthma hazard index of zero and previously was not known to be a respiratory sensitizing agent. The implications of this finding for the refinement of quantitative structural analysis of asthmagenic chemicals are discussed.</AbstractText>
